    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d344">

                <pb facs="0392" n="380" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg380"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 European War 1939/10–143:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Prime Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Churchill</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to President Roosevelt </hi><anchor
                        n="11" xml:id="d344-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-09-30">September 30, 1943</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>[427.]<anchor n="12" xml:id="d344-f2"/> Your No. 363.<anchor n="13"
                        xml:id="d344-f3"/> I agree that we should make a joint announcement but
                    would it not be a good chance of getting Uncle Joe in too? It is clear now, from
                    correction of Molotov’s message,<anchor n="14" xml:id="d344-f4"/> that he does
                    accept the Italians as co-belligerents. It is true we may lose a few days in
                    communicating with Moscow, but this delay seems relatively unimportant compared
                    with value of Russian participation.</p>
                <p>If you agree, would you put it to Stalin in the form that we wish an announcement
                    of the kind made; will he join with us in making it, or would he prefer us to go
                    ahead without him? Of course we should consider any drafting alterations he
                    might wish to propose.</p>
                <p>I myself would like to see several changes, and my immediately following
                        telegram<anchor n="15" xml:id="d344-f5"/> embodies these. If you see no
                    objection to them would you, if you agree, approach Stalin and put text to him
                    in this form.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
